  "message": "Write velocity output in the input frame on rotated-pole meshes\n\nWhen the momentum equations are solved in a rotated spherical frame\n(ICS +/-22/24 with a fort.rotm rotation, IFSPROTS=1), the state\nvelocities UU2/VV2 hold components along the rotated coordinate axes.\nThe fort.61/62/63/64 writers passed them through untransformed, so\nvelocity time series and station output carried rotated-frame\ncomponents against geographic coordinates - directions wrong by up to\n~90 degrees near the rotated poles, while every scalar (elevation,\nspeed, maxvel) looked correct. Meteorological output and the harmonic\nanalysis (which back-rotates before its least-squares update) were\nalready in the geographic input frame, so the file set was internally\ninconsistent.\n\nVelocity output is now re-expressed in geographic east/north before it\nis written: UU2_GEO/VV2_GEO are allocated only when the rotated frame\nis in use, bound to the global and station velocity descriptors in\nplace of UU2/VV2, and refreshed via the existing DRVMAP2DSPVEC inverse\ntransform at most once per time step and only on steps where a\nvelocity output is actually due.\n\nResolves #510",
